<style>
  .drawer { position: fixed; inset: 0 auto 0 0; width: min(20rem, 90vw); transform: translateX(-100%); transition: transform 180ms ease; }
  .drawer.is-open { transform: translateX(0); }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .drawer { transition: none; } }
</style>
<aside class="drawer is-open" aria-label="Navigation">Menu</aside>
```
The fixed drawer moves over the page; it does not ask article content to reflow on every frame.

```html
<button id="play">Play explanation</button>
<div id="cursor" aria-hidden="true">●</div>
<script>
  const cursor = document.querySelector('#cursor');
  const control = document.querySelector('#play');
  let motion;
  control.addEventListener('click', () => {
    motion?.cancel();
    motion = cursor.animate(
      [{ transform: 'translateX(0)' }, { transform: 'translateX(12rem)' }],
      { duration: 900, fill: 'both', easing: 'ease-in-out' }
    );
  });
</script>
```
The returned animation can later be paused, reversed, cancelled, or inspected by the same controller.
